Hi Javid,

Hope you had a wonderful break.

I had a relaxing yet very busy week in work and meetings.

Here are the details of the work that I did:

  *
Already send email about SS vs NUM which Kurt responded that he is happy to=
 wait till you come back. Let me know what will be the next steps.
  *
Handed over the SBS query to Krishna after adding few fields to match the c=
ustomer portal schema.
  *
Had a discussion with Deepti about the python code and next steps in the au=
tomated emails campaign.
     *
On Tuesday Deepti told me that the Marketing team want the automation to be=
 done with Hubspot and not python. As per Deepti's conversation with Kurt, =
it was emphasised that the marketing automation will be done through their =
existing systems for ownership. Let me know what the next steps will be.
     *
We also had a meeting today about the future campaigns but in my opinion ma=
rketing team is not clear on the direction so they will come back to us wit=
h clarity.
  *
I also updated the capability assessment adding comments to the areas which=
 are different.
  *
There was a requirement given by Kurt to display data of sales of EV Techni=
cal specification given free. We need to monitor who purchased those standa=
rds. Output would be in Excel file refreshed weekly.
     *
I gathered the data and put it in a Power BI report as data refresh in exce=
l from SQL is complicated and done through ADF and power automate.
  *
I also had a meeting with Richard about DMR-800. I have not committed any d=
eadline to that project but i am estimating that I would have something by =
the end of this month.
     *
I also started working on this report.
  *
There were some BAU enquiries about Royalties calculators from Shannon to a=
dd and manage users which I have responded and resolved.
  *
I have already updated the follow up communications course and are up to da=
te.
  *
Other updates are that I am planning 2 weeks leave in Jan 2025 potentially =
at the last part of school holidays. I will discuss this in our 1:1 but thi=
s is just a heads up.

Some responses to the feedbacks:

  *
As a response to the constructive feedback on DMR-800, I would like to say =
that there was nothing done without prior to the meeting with Richard. Conn=
ect was a major blocker agreed by Richard. After the meeting, I was clear o=
n the other requirements about the report along with the data points as a w=
ork around. If I would have started working without any discussion and clar=
ity, I would have to redo the work based on clarity of the requirements.
  *
About the RG report, I can say that first the email draft, then the Teams m=
essage draft went through your approval not just 1 time but multiple times =
so i don't see any issue with my communication.
  *
I have a positive mindset and always ready to help out people from my work =
and other things. You can ask other team members as well on this. I am good=
 when I have work and challenges. I have done this through my almost 4.5 ye=
ars in Standards.

I hope to restart work with complete passion and enthusiasm when I come bac=
k on 14/10.
Anything urgent, you can reach out to me on teams or WhatsApp.

Thanks,

Fahad


